Q: How to structure reusable response models in FastAPI for multiple content formats? A: <pre><code>from fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException
from pydantic import BaseModel, Field
from typing import List, Optional
from uuid import uuid4

app = FastAPI(title=&quot;Simple FastAPI CRUD Example&quot;)

# -----------------------------
# Models
# -----------------------------
class Item(BaseModel):
    id: Optional[str] = None
    name: str = Field(..., min_length=2, max_length=50)
    description: Optional[str] = None
    price: float = Field(..., gt=0)
    quantity: int = Field(default=0, ge=0)

class ItemUpdate(BaseModel):
    name: Optional[str]
    description: Optional[str]
    price: Optional[float]
    quantity: Optional[int]

# -----------------------------
# Fake Database
# -----------------------------
db: List[Item] = []

# -----------------------------
# Routes
# -----------------------------
@app.get(&quot;/&quot;)
def root():
    return {&quot;message&quot;: &quot;Welcome to FastAPI CRUD API&quot;}

@app.post(&quot;/items&quot;, response_model=Item)
def create_item(item: Item):
    item.id = str(uuid4())
    db.append(item)
    return item

@app.get(&quot;/items&quot;, response_model=List[Item])
def get_all_items():
    return db

@app.get(&quot;/items/{item_id}&quot;, response_model=Item)
def get_item(item_id: str):
    for item in db:
        if item.id == item_id:
            return item
    raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=&quot;Item not found&quot;)

@app.put(&quot;/items/{item_id}&quot;, response_model=Item)
def update_item(item_id: str, updated: ItemUpdate):
    for index, item in enumerate(db):
        if item.id == item_id:
            updated_data = item.dict()
            update_fields = updated.dict(exclude_unset=True)
            updated_data.update(update_fields)
            db[index] = Item(**updated_data)
            return db[index]
    raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=&quot;Item not found&quot;)

@app.delete(&quot;/items/{item_id}&quot;)
def delete_item(item_id: str):
    for index, item in enumerate(db):
        if item.id == item_id:
            db.pop(index)
            return {&quot;message&quot;: &quot;Item deleted successfully&quot;}
    raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail=&quot;Item not found&quot;)

# -----------------------------
# Extra Features
# -----------------------------
@app.get(&quot;/items/search/&quot;)
def search_items(min_price: float = 0, max_price: float = 10000):
    results = [
        item for item in db
        if min_price &lt;= item.price &lt;= max_price
    ]
    return results

@app.get(&quot;/items/low-stock/&quot;)
def low_stock(threshold: int = 5):
    return [item for item in db if item.quantity &lt;= threshold]

@app.delete(&quot;/items&quot;)
def clear_all_items():
    db.clear()
    return {&quot;message&quot;: &quot;All items removed&quot;}

# -----------------------------
# Run Instructions
# -----------------------------
&quot;&quot;&quot;
Run this app using:

uvicorn filename:app --reload

Then open:
http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

FastAPI automatically provides Swagger UI.
&quot;&quot;&quot;
</code></pre>

